<p>The U.S. Court of International Trade ruled 2-1 against President Trump’s 10% global tariff on Thursday, finding Section 122 of the Trade Act of 1974 did not justify the across-the-board duties. The panel granted relief to the two small businesses and Washington state that sued, but did not issue a nationwide injunction; it ordered implementation within five days and refunds for the successful importers.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/0FYhwUTUp2CQ42NtUlvHlAJsbT4qK4nbI72jV5AiRnppZIu6e8lWNBfTwMzScYkr7XXRQh87ZPmHnagSVgqnfz89w-PXsYLPjmSNux3dFPwX_ZEnQsDz-2g-D8zkTpHxeznaBfaRbvwdQLAHH6_XMrQvSISxlkJPVYZQMuCGaWi3TYK55LgYTCT1MuKPLv0ucXa55jLPzAOuNxKnrwqdsf6j-RZxBP0zxs8jp7n2-znpmUxeFtWxjN-wp1FsWZmlrALMcI2Fv6_9UMbBgg' alt='U.S. President Donald Trump speaks during a Small Business Summit in the East Room at the White House in Washington, D.C., U.S., May 4, 2026.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Plaintiffs named: The two private plaintiffs were toy company Basic Fun! and spice importer Burlap &amp; Barrel, both of which challenged the Section 122 duties.</li><li>State standing: Washington state submitted evidence that the University of Washington, a public research institution, paid tariffs, while the court found other states were not importers that had paid or could have paid the duties.</li><li>Separate duties: The trade court decision did not affect Trump’s sector-specific tariffs on steel, aluminum and autos.</li><li>EU deadline: Trump separately warned the European Union to implement trade-deal terms by July 4 or face tariffs at “much higher levels”.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Small-business plaintiffs: The challengers argued that the February tariffs were an attempt to sidestep a U.S. Supreme Court decision that struck down Trump’s 2025 tariffs under the International Emergency Economic Powers Act. (<a href='https://news.rthk.hk/rthk/en/component/k2/1853952-20260508.htm'>RTHK</a>)</li><li>Dissenting judge: One judge on the three-member panel said the court acted prematurely in granting victory to the small-business plaintiffs. (<a href='https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/may/07/trump-global-tariffs-trade-court-ruling'>The Guardian</a>)</li><li>Reported administration strategy: El Financiero reported that the global tariff had been expected to serve as a temporary measure while the government explored more durable legal bases for tariffs. (<a href='https://www.elfinanciero.com.mx/mundo/2026/05/07/dan-reves-judicial-a-trump-tribunal-de-eu-bloquea-su-arancel-global-del-10-por-ser-ilegal/'>El Financiero</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.lemonde.fr/en/economy/article/2026/05/08/us-trade-court-rules-against-trump-s-global-10-tariff_6753235_19.html'>US trade court rules against Trump&#x27;s global 10% tariff</a> - lemonde.fr</li><li><a href='https://www.ndtv.com/world-news/us-trade-court-rules-against-trumps-10-global-tariffs-11464829#publisher=newsstand'>&#x27;Misguided&#x27;: US Court Rules Against Trump&#x27;s 10% Global Tariffs</a> - ndtv.com</li><li><a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/economy/2026/5/7/us-trade-court-rules-against-trumps-10-percent-global-tariffs'>US trade court rules against Trump’s 10 percent global tariffs</a> - aljazeera.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/may/07/trump-global-tariffs-trade-court-ruling'>US trade court rules against Trump’s 10% global tariffs</a> - theguardian.com</li><li><a href='https://www.dw.com/en/us-court-deals-fresh-blow-to-trump-s-10-global-tariff-policy/a-77088575'>US court deals fresh blow to Trump&#x27;s 10% global tariff policy</a> - dw.com</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/us-trade-court-rules-against-trumps-10-global-tariffs'>US trade court rules Trump tariffs illegal, but issues narrow block</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/federal-court-rules-against-new-global-tariffs-trump-imposed-after-loss-at-supreme-court/article70953690.ece'>Fede